            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Larger than the machine's footprint, not equal to it. A mat sized exactly to the treadmill puts the feet near the weakest edges and leaves no margin if it shifts. Extend it behind the deck to cover the run-off area, which is also where sweat lands, and make sure it covers where the machine sits when folded as well as when in use.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are horse stall mats good for treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "They are the value option people who know keep recommending — thick, very dense recycled rubber sold in large sheets at a fraction of the price per square foot of fitness-branded equivalents. Two caveats: they are extremely heavy to manoeuvre, and they have a strong rubber smell for the first few weeks, so air one outdoors before putting it in a bedroom.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
